{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "id": "gen-261",
   "subject": "Inquiry Regarding Automated Appointment Reminder Delivery and Customization",
   "body": "Dear Support Team, We are writing to request assistance with our automated appointment notifications. Several patients have informed our front desk staff that they are no longer receiving text message or email reminders prior to their visits. Additionally, we would like to update the wording and timing of these messages to better suit our clinic's protocols. Please advise on how we can verify why these messages are failing to deliver and how to access the template settings. Sincerely, Front Desk Team",
   "id": "gen-261"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-262",
   "subject": "URGENT: Potential Data Exposure in Compliance Archive",
   "body": "We discovered that historical patient records in our backup archives may have been viewable by an unauthorized user account. We need to lock this down immediately and review the audit logs. Please contact me right away.",
   "id": "gen-262"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-263",
   "subject": "Confused about batch claim validation errors",
   "body": "Hello, I am trying to push out the weekly insurance claims for our providers, but the system keeps flagging a bunch of them with error code V-402 right before batch submission. I am not really sure what this error means or how I am supposed to fix the validation issues on these specific forms. Could someone please walk me through how to correct them so we can get our claims sent off to the clearinghouse? Thank you.",
   "id": "gen-263"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-264",
   "subject": "Apologies - incorrect medication transmitted to pharmacy",
   "body": "Hello support, I am so sorry to bother you, but I made an error earlier this afternoon while handling an out-of-stock alert for a patient. I accidentally transmitted the wrong therapeutic alternative to the pharmacy instead of the intended substitute. Could you please help me reverse this transmission or advise on how to properly send the correct medication update to the pharmacist? Thank you so much for your help.",
   "id": "gen-264"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-265",
   "subject": "Request for Assistance Updating Practice NPI and Provider Identifiers",
   "body": "Dear Support Team, We recently underwent some administrative restructuring and need to update our practice's billing address, tax ID, and provider NPI numbers within the system. We attempted to make these changes under the practice settings menu, but we noticed that recent outgoing insurance claims are still reflecting our old information. Could you please provide guidance on how to ensure these updates propagate correctly to all billing modules? Best regards, Practice Administration",
   "id": "gen-265"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-266",
   "subject": "Need to update practice tax ID and location address on claims",
   "body": "Hi team,\n\nWe moved to a new building last month and updated our practice address and tax ID in the main settings page. However, looking at the claims we submitted yesterday, the clearinghouse is still rejecting them because they show our old location details.\n\nI tried toggling the primary location switch under the administrative profile and re-saving, but it didn't change anything on the outgoing forms. Can you tell me if there is a separate place where billing identifiers need to be refreshed?\n\nThanks,\nAdmin",
   "id": "gen-266"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-267",
   "subject": "Having trouble processing medication substitution alerts",
   "body": "I am trying to handle an out-of-stock notification for a patient's script, but the system keeps locking up every time I attempt to select an alternative therapeutic agent from the dropdown menu. This is the third time this week a pharmacy alert workflow has failed on me, and it is holding up my afternoon schedule. Please look into why this substitution module is lagging and let me know how to push this prescription through immediately.",
   "id": "gen-267"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-268",
   "subject": "Assistance Required for Updating Pharmacy Out-of-Stock Notification Preferences",
   "body": "Dear Support Team,\n\nI am writing to request guidance on managing medication substitution workflows and out-of-stock alerts within our patient management system. Earlier today, one of our physicians attempted to switch an unavailable prescription to an alternative agent, but the notification flags did not route properly to the designated pharmacy.\n\nWe have checked the provider settings and ensured that our local pharmacy directory is up to date, but the substitution messaging tabs appear greyed out on certain patient profiles. Could you please provide instructions on how our front desk and clinical staff can correctly configure these alert pathways so future notifications transmit without error?\n\nThank you for your time and assistance.\n\nSincerely,\nFront Office Coordinator",
   "id": "gen-268"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-269",
   "subject": "Question regarding batch insurance claim generation and clearinghouse errors",
   "body": "Hello, I am sorry to reach out about this, but I am having some trouble getting our daily insurance claims to batch correctly for electronic submission. Every time I try to generate the file, the system stops and gives me an unhandled validation error that I haven't seen before. I tried clearing my browser cache and restarting the billing module, but the same message keeps appearing. Could someone please help me figure out what is causing this so I can get our claims sent out today? Thank you.",
   "id": "gen-269"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-270",
   "subject": "Lab orders keep getting rejected",
   "body": "My electronic lab requisitions are getting kicked back by the reference lab all morning with generic formatting errors, and your interface gives zero details on what is wrong. Fix this immediately so I can actually send my orders.",
   "id": "gen-270"
  }
 ]
}
